# OGMBC Web App

Brief: PHP + Bootstrap site for OGMBC consultants (audit, IFRS, advisory).  
Open the site via a local PHP server (XAMPP / WAMP / MAMP) and use the admin pages for CMS tasks.

Quick links
- Main entry: [index.php](index.php)
- Ratios tool: [ratios.php](ratios.php) (see `RATIOS` constant and [`downloadPdf`](ratios.php))
- DB config: [includes/database.php](includes/database.php) (uses `$connection`)
- Mail & helpers: [includes/functions.php](includes/functions.php) (contains `insert_categories` usage)
- Header(s): [includes/header.php](includes/header.php), [includes/header-1.php](includes/header-1.php)
- Footer: [includes/footer.php](includes/footer.php)
- CSS: [resources/css/style.css](resources/css/style.css)
- JS: [resources/js/main.js](resources/js/main.js)
- Admin example: [admin/categories.php](admin/categories.php)

Prerequisites
1. PHP 8+ and MySQL (XAMPP/WAMP/MAMP recommended).  
2. Composer (for PHPMailer).  
3. Modern browser for client-side features (html2canvas/jsPDF used in [ratios.php](ratios.php)).

Setup (local)
1. Copy the repository into your web server document root, for example:
   - Windows XAMPP: C:\xampp\htdocs\ogmbc\ogmbc-web-app
2. Start Apache and MySQL (XAMPP Control Panel).

Database
1. Create a database named `ogmbc` (matches [includes/database.php](includes/database.php)):
   - Using phpMyAdmin or CLI:
     - CREATE DATABASE ogmbc;
2. Create required tables (posts, users, etc.) or import a provided SQL dump if available. The app expects `posts` and `users` for the blog features used in [index.php](index.php) and [post_detail.php](post_detail.php).

Composer / PHPMailer
1. From project root run:
   ```sh
   composer require phpmailer/phpmailer

2. Edit includes/functions.php:
Set $environment to production when ready.
Configure SMTP credentials (Host, Username, Password) as commented in file.
Configuration notes

DB connection uses includes/database.php -> variable $connection.
Email sending logic and environment selection live in includes/functions.php.
Floating WhatsApp buttons use the number +971502923136 across the site (see index.php and other pages).
Ratio calculator: client-side only, stores saved reports in browser localStorage; exports via html2canvas + jsPDF (loaded in includes/header-1.php).
Run / View

Open in browser:
http://localhost/ogmbc-web-app/index.php
Admin

Admin area files are in admin/ (e.g. admin/categories.php). Ensure proper authentication before exposing to public.
Troubleshooting

Blank page / errors: enable PHP error display in php.ini or check Apache error log.
SMTP issues: ensure credentials and port are correct; for Gmail use App Password and TLS (see comments in includes/functions.php).
JS features (PDF download) require html2canvas and jsPDF — included in headers.
Maintenance

Centralize repeated contact info if desired: search for phone/email occurrences (e.g., index.php and includes/footer.php) and update accordingly.
